<title>USA: ARCO mulls cuts, transfers at headquarters.</title>
<headline>ARCO mulls cuts, transfers at headquarters.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Los Angeles-based Atlantic Richfield Co.(ARCO) is planning to restructure its corporate headquarters, a move which could result in layoffs and relocations.</p>
<p>A spokesman declined to specify the extent or timing of the cuts, but industry sources said the cuts could be substantial.</p>
<p>ARCO, the seventh largest oil company in the U.S., employs about 22,800 employees worldwide, with 1,400 located in Los Angeles County and 2,800 placed among its five business units in Texas.</p>
<p>The company is mulling the restructuring as part of ongoing review of staff begun earlier this year.</p>
<p>((David Brinkerhoff, Los Angeles bureau +1 213 380 2014))</p>
